# Git identity — santoshimz

For this repository (`screenwriting-tool`), always commit and push as **santoshimz**.

## Commit author

Do **not** change global or local `git config`. Set the author per commit:

```bash
git commit --author="santoshimz <santoshimz@gmail.com>" -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Your message here.

EOF
)"
```

## Push remote

Use the SSH host alias that authenticates as santoshimz:

```bash
git remote set-url origin git@github-santoshimz:santoshimz/screenwriting-tool.git
git push -u origin main
```

If `origin` already uses `github-santoshimz`, push normally.

## Scope

- Applies to all commits in this repo unless the user explicitly asks for a different identity.
- Never commit `drafts/`, `.venv/`, or user screenplay PDFs.
